&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2018&lt;/strong&gt;: Secured Pre-series A funding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2019&lt;/strong&gt;: Expanded operations to India, Southeast Asia, and the Americas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2020&lt;/strong&gt;: Won the NASSCOM-DSCI Excellence Award for Security Product Company of the Year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2021&lt;/strong&gt;: Raised $7M in Series A funding led by MassMutual Ventures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Awards &amp;amp; Recognition&lt;/strong&gt;: Won NetApp Excellerator&#39;s &quot;Best Growth Strategy Award,&quot; CloudSEK XVigil joined NVIDIA Inception Program, and won the NASSCOM Emerge 50 Cybersecurity Award.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2025&lt;/strong&gt;: Secured $19 million in funding led by Tenacity Ventures, Commvault.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CloudSEK is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Customer Threat Advisor&lt;/strong&gt; to help customers convert cyber intelligence into clear action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a customer-facing security role for someone who understands cyber threats and can explain them clearly to CISOs, security teams, and business stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits at the intersection of customer success, threat intelligence, AI security, infrastructure vulnerability management, and security consulting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Customer Threat Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will ensure that customers clearly understand the threats affecting them and the value CloudSEK is delivering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review threat intelligence findings for assigned accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-priority incidents that need customer attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain the business impact of threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share critical incident updates with CISOs and security teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up on important incidents until there is action or closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conduct Weekly Incident Triage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with analysts to review customer incidents every week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review critical and high-severity incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize incidents based on customer context and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear customer-ready summaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure important incidents are not missed or buried in reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track which incidents were reported, acknowledged, and actioned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as a Security Consultant to Customers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should enjoy working like a consultant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the customer’s environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask the right questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate issues with analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simplify complex threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect findings to business risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise customers on the next best action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is not about passing information from one team to another. It is about helping customers understand risk and act with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can understand cyber threats and explain them clearly to customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The person should have interest or experience across:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Threat Intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dark web and deep web threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credential leaks and stealer logs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brand impersonation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data leaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attack surface exposures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud and internet-facing risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI security risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Third-party and vendor risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate should have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–7 years of experience in cybersecurity, threat intelligence, SOC, customer success, technical account management, security consulting, or security operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of security incidents and business risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate with both analysts and CISOs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity to investigate and understand threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use AI tools responsibly to improve investigation, summarization, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Success Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The most important success metric for this role will be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of successful incidents triaged and reported to customers.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Other metrics include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Number of critical incidents proactively communicated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Number of incidents acknowledged or actioned by customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality of customer-ready incident summaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality of weekly incident reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer feedback from CISOs and security teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adoption of relevant CloudSEK modules and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribution to renewals and expansions through demonstrated value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A successful Customer Threat Advisor ensures that every assigned customer clearly understands:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What threats were discovered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which incidents matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why they matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What action should be taken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What value CloudSEK delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best people in this role will not wait for escalations. They will proactively find value, explain risk, and help customers act before the issue becomes a crisis.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits of Joining CloudSEK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
