&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you have a strong background and/or are actively passionate about &lt;strong&gt;offensive security and threat intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you love to &lt;strong&gt;ELI5 complex technical findings&lt;/strong&gt; for diverse stakeholders, from SOC teams to CXOs and &lt;strong&gt;have excellent communication &amp;amp; presentation skills&lt;/strong&gt; to drive home business impact from these with confidence in high-stakes engagements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are you hands-on with &lt;strong&gt;AI-driven automation &lt;/strong&gt;in scaling your technical capacity?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you love taking&lt;strong&gt; end-to-end responsibility for outcomes&lt;/strong&gt; and thrive in a &lt;strong&gt;fast-paced, dynamic, self-driven and high-volume consulting environment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CloudSEK’s &lt;strong&gt;Security Consulting Threat Research &amp;amp; Intelligence for Key Enablement (STRIKE)&lt;/strong&gt; Division operates at the intersection of threat research, consulting, and business enablement. As a Security Consultant for the MEA market, you will wear multiple hats: a &lt;strong&gt;trusted technical advisor&lt;/strong&gt; during trials, a &lt;strong&gt;threat researcher&lt;/strong&gt; uncovering insights tailored to regional risks, a &lt;strong&gt;consulting partner&lt;/strong&gt; driving adoption through clear business impact to help position CloudSEK to our client partners as a strategic ally in their cyber resilience journey, and a community builder to expand CloudSEKs footprint and visibility in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Value Translation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead new business &lt;strong&gt;trials and proof-of-capability (POC) engagements&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring successful demonstration of technical outcomes and translation of business impact by presenting CloudSEK’s AI-driven predictive threat intelligence and infrastructure security capabilities to executives and security teams, bridging technical depth with business relevance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat Research &amp;amp; Regional Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively track the Cyber Threat Landscape for the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and track &lt;strong&gt;region-specific threats&lt;/strong&gt; in MEA across government, telecom, BFSI, and enterprise sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce &lt;strong&gt;custom intelligence briefs, RFP responses, and exposure reports&lt;/strong&gt; that highlight CloudSEK’s proactive value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Ecosystem Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with &lt;strong&gt;partner security consultants&lt;/strong&gt; to deliver onboarding, enablement, and co-selling activities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a &lt;strong&gt;regional subject matter expert (SME)&lt;/strong&gt; for partners, contextualizing CloudSEK’s value within MEA threat landscapes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thought Leadership &amp;amp; Outreach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively build the CloudSEK community in the region by participating, contributing to as well as initiating and driving community events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to CloudSEK’s &lt;strong&gt;lead generation efforts&lt;/strong&gt; by creating research-driven reports and customer-facing intelligence insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent CloudSEK at &lt;strong&gt;regional forums, webinars, and customer workshops&lt;/strong&gt;, strengthening brand credibility.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have at least 3+ years of relevant industry experience in client-facing roles and account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Been part of the Cyber Security domain - Mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to think logically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interact confidently with clients to identify what the security problem is and explain the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to prioritize workload and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoys solving problems and displays an eagerness to learn new technologies/skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team handling capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to juggle multiple account management projects at a time, while maintaining sharp attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and able to thrive in a start-up culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Expectations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mid to senior-level experience in information security or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate level of knowledge in cybersecurity.&lt;/li&gt;
